San Felice Circeo is a town and comune in the province of Latina, in the Lazio region of central Italy. It was an ancient city called Circeii. It is one of I Borghi più belli d'Italia ("The most beautiful villages of Italy"). It is included in the Circeo National Park. Sites include the Grotta Guattari, one of the oldest Neanderthal sites in Italy, in which remains of nine Neanderthals were discovered. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Felice_Circeo?utm_source=openai))

The town is located on the western coast of Italy, perched on the shores of the Tyrrhenian Sea, southwest of Rome. ([hellomondo.com](https://www.hellomondo.com/italy/san-felice-circeo/?utm_source=openai))

The Circeo National Park was established in 1934 to preserve the last remains of the Pontine Marshes, which were being reclaimed in that period. It is the only national park in Italy to occupy only a plain and coastal area. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circeo_National_Park?utm_source=openai))

The park can be divided into five main habitats: the forest, the promontory, the littoral dune, the humid area, and the island of Zannone. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circeo_National_Park?utm_source=openai))

The promontory of Circeo, with a maximum height of 541m, is a Mesozoic limestone-dolomite massif with a peculiar island shape, and gives its name to the whole park. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circeo_National_Park?utm_source=openai))

The promontory is believed to be the ancient Eea Island, home of Circe, the Goddess who kept Ulysses as a prisoner, according to Homer's Odyssey. The shape of the land which stretches into the sea seems to be that of the Goddess, lying motionless on the beach. ([theitalianblog.net](https://theitalianblog.net/san-felice-circeo/?utm_source=openai))

The Circeo National Park includes a 22km-long coastal sand strip, from the limestone cliffs of the Mount Circeo, in correspondence of the Torre Paola watchtower, up to Capo Portiere. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circeo_National_Park?utm_source=openai))

The park is home to a vast wildlife of aquatic birds, as well as to rare species such as the marsh turtle. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circeo_National_Park?utm_source=openai))

The park also includes the island of Zannone, a small island belonging to the Ponziano archipelago, annexed to the park in 1979. Uninhabited, it is covered by woods of oaks and holm oaks, and is the only island in the archipelago to have kept its original vegetation cover. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circeo_National_Park?utm_source=openai))

The park is managed by the Ministero dell'Ambiente. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circeo_National_Park?utm_source=openai))

The park's official website is http://www.parks.it/parco.nazionale.circeo/Eindex.html. ([en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circeo_National_Park?utm_source=openai))

